<<!DOCTYPE "memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki" "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext">>

This carrier holds one structure `lares meme check` refuses ON PURPOSE, the same fault
`control-set.mem` carries, here beside a block check that otherwise closes clean:
`<<^ code="&#x0017;">>` carries ETB, which `$carrier-sila` mints only behind a computed, verified
check, never a bare literal. Declared in `corpus/must-flag.txt`. A call site further down also
takes the equals spelling over the colon — a grammar-class PREFERENCE `--grammar` reports, not a
fault this file asserts, and no declaration names it.

<<^ code="&#x0001;" from="?" -> to="lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/example">>

<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

A body whose close carries a block check.

<<^ code="&#x0003;">>ni:///sha-256;j1yWiREtBrtyp0nn-14FCoVTGPrIYWoom0NGp-WrjOE

<<^ code="&#x0017;">> ni:///sha-256;AAAA1234BBBB5678CCCC9012DDDD3456EEEE7890FFFF

<<^>>

<<~ sigil bracket=[[a bracketed value]] single='a single quoted value'>>

<<^ code="&#x0004;" -> to="?">>

A parameter takes the colon spelling as well as the equals spelling: a call reads a bracketed
or quoted value the same way under either. A definition's own parameter list refuses the
equals spelling --- only the colon separates a default there.

<<~ kue voice:Mischief-Muse key:"a value carrying spaces" held:[[a bracketed value]]>>
